   "mayor": null,
   "motion_no": 12
  },
  {
   "body": "Council",
   "motion": "that the mayoral candidates be given 3 minutes to speak during their interviews if there are 10 candidates or less, and 2 minutes to speak if there are 11 candidates or more with up to an additional 5 minutes per candidate to engage in questions from the council and any council member that is formally running for mayor cannot ask questions during those 5 minutes",
   "motion_type": "Other",
   "result": "5-0 Pass",
   "mover": "Bryant Brown",
   "seconder": "Heidi Robinson",
   "aye": [
    "Bonnie Billings",
    "Paul Glover",
    "Heidi Robinson",
    "Bryant Brown",
    "Dustin Gettel"
   ],
   "nay": [],
   "abstain": [],
   "absent": [],
   "recuse": [],
   "names_recorded": true,
   "mayor_voted": false,
   "mayor": null,
   "motion_no": 13
  },
  {
   "body": "Council",
   "motion": "in the event of an initial mayoral vote resulting in four or more candidates, a round-robin coin toss process be used to determine which candidate will face the one with the most city council votes, or which two tied candidates will face each other in a final vote. The City Recorder will toss a coin on behalf of each candidate against every other candidate in a round. The City Recorder will assign each candidate a side of the coin prior to each coin toss. At the end of each round, the candidate(s) with the fewest wins will be eliminated. This process will continue until only one candidate rema",
   "motion_type": "Procedural/Administrative",
   "result": "5-0 Pass",
   "mover": "Bryant Brown",
   "seconder": "Heidi Robinson",
   "aye": [
    "Bonnie Billings",
    "Paul Glover",
    "Heidi Robinson",
    "Bryant Brown",
    "Dustin Gettel"
   ],
   "nay": [],
   "abstain": [],
   "absent": [],
   "recuse": [],
   "names_recorded": true,
   "mayor_voted": false,
   "mayor": null,
   "motion_no": 14
  },
  {
   "body": "Council",
   "motion": "that, for each round of voting, council members receive a ballot with their name on it to select their chosen candidate. After each vote, the City Recorder and City Attorney will collect and count the ballots. The City Recorder will announce the vote count and place the ballots in an envelope for that round",
   "motion_type": "Other",
   "result": "5-0 Pass",
   "mover": "Bryant Brown",
   "seconder": "Heidi Robinson",
